1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,060
Previously on The Big Bang Theory...

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,840
We now pronounce you husband and wife!

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:12,050
I love this part!

4
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:13,650
Me, too!

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:17,390
I have strongly mixed feelings!

6
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:21,920
So, Howard's really in space, huh?

7
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,820
Mm-hmm, International Space Station.

8
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:25,990
250 miles that way.

9
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:28,720
Right now, Howard's staring down at our planet

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,250
like a tiny Jewish Greek god.

11
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:35,320
Zeusowitz.

12
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,680
I must admit,

13
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:39,180
I can't help but feel a twinge of envy.

14
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:40,650
He can look out the window

15
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:42,850
and see the majesty of the universe

16
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:44,950
unfolding before his eyes.

17
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,450
His dim, uncomprehending eyes.

18
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:54,810
It's like a cat in an airport carrying case.

19
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,480
You know, it's not exactly glamorous up there.

20
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,930
The water that the astronauts drink

21
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:02,430
is made from each other's recycled urine.

22
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,210
Must be nice.

23
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,950
Nobody wants anything that comes out of me.

24
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:15,950
I wonder what he's doing right this very second.

25
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,670
Mm, conducting experiments in zero gravity.

26
00:01:18,670 --> 00:01:21,140
Peering through his telescope at the birth of the cosmos.

27
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,650
Whatever it is, we know his life will never be the same.

28
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:28,710
Howard! Can you hear me?!

29
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:31,410
I can hear you without the phone!

30
00:01:32,310 --> 00:01:33,810
Don't be snippy.

31
00:01:33,810 --> 00:01:36,370
I'm just excited to talk to my baby!

32
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:39,070
I'm excited to talk to you, too.

33
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:41,810
So, what's this mishegas about you moving out

34
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:44,690
to go live with the little Polish girl?!

35
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,880
How about calling her my wife?

36
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,510
Wives don't take boys from their mothers.

37
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:53,390
They do. That's why we marry them!

38
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:57,440
I just hope I'm not dead from a broken heart

39
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,110
before you get back.

40
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:00,670
Ma, please.

41
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:03,910
Everyone from NASA is listening to this phone call.

42
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:07,510
Good. They should know what a horrible son you are!

43
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:10,630
Okay, Ma, great talking to you! Gotta go!

44
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,230
Well... space is ruined.

45
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:51,370
This is so exciting.

46
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,060
Soon, my upper lip will be the same fake blonde

47
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:56,740
as my beautiful best friend.

48
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,580
Hey, this is my natural hair color.

49
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,000
Now.

50
00:03:04,970 --> 00:03:07,140
So, does Sheldon have anything special

51
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,770
planned for you tomorrow night?

52
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:11,580
Oh, yes. According to the Relationship Agreement,

53
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,330
on the anniversary of our first date,

54
00:03:13,330 --> 00:03:14,880
he must take me to a nice dinner,

55
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,130
ask about my day

56
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:18,120
and engage in casual physical contact

57
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,740
that a disinterested onlooker might mistake for intimacy.

58
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,370
That's hot.

59
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,690
You kids better use protection.

60
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:29,920
How long does this stay on?

61
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,040
Just a couple of minutes.

62
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,570
You've really never done this before?

63
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:34,870
Once in high school, but I dozed off

64
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:37,570
and woke up with second-degree chemical burns on my face.

65
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:40,040
Oh, my gosh, that's awful.

66
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,470
The other kids make fun of you?

67
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:42,650
No, I had a cover story;

68
00:03:42,650 --> 00:03:44,280
I told everyone it was herpes.

69
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,390
So, how's everything going with you and Leonard?

70
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:50,510
I don't know, it's still kind of weird.

71
00:03:50,550 --> 00:03:52,820
We haven't really recovered since he proposed to me

72
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:54,110
in the middle of sex.

73
00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:55,980
Oh. Boo-hoo.

74
00:03:57,050 --> 00:03:58,770
If Sheldon proposed to me during sex,

75
00:03:58,770 --> 00:03:59,860
my ovaries would grab on to him

76
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,260
and never let go.

77
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:11,850
Leonard, where do you stand on the anthropic principle?

78
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:12,890
Interesting question.

79
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:14,220
On the one hand, I always thought...

80
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,550
You don't even know what it is, do you?

81
00:04:17,050 --> 00:04:20,930
The anthropic principle states that if we wish to explain

82
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:23,220
why our universe exists the way it does,

83
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,070
the answer is that it must have qualities

84
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:28,540
that allow intelligent creatures to arise

85
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,680
who are capable of asking the question.

86
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,980
As I am doing so eloquently right now.

87
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,710
I know what the anthropic principle is.

88
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,000
Of course. I just explained it to you.

89
00:04:40,970 --> 00:04:43,210
Now, where do you stand on it?

90
00:04:43,210 --> 00:04:45,360
- Where do you stand on it? - Strongly pro.

91
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,090
Then I believe that God created the world in six days,

92
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:50,580
and on the seventh, he made you to annoy me.

93
00:04:55,230 --> 00:04:56,310
Hey, guys.

94
00:04:56,310 --> 00:04:57,390
Yeah, wait, Raj,

95
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:59,760
where do you stand on the anthropic principle?

96
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,860
- I'm all for it. - Attaboy!

97
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:03,190
Well, hang on. Why do you believe

98
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:04,970
that he knows what it is and I don't?

99
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:07,640
Oh, Leonard. Let's not take a saw

100
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,240
to the branch we're sitting on, shall we?

101
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:12,560
Hey, uh, if you guys are free tonight,

102
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,900
I heard about a SPA where you soak your feet

103
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,460
in a pool full of little fish

104
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,470
that eat all the dead skin right off them.

105
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,760
I don't need to tell you, in Los Angeles,

106
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,320
sandal season is year round.

107
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,470
- Actually, I'm hanging out with Penny. - Oh, okay.

108
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:30,210
Sounds like it's me and you, Sheldon.

109
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:32,680
How about we sic some guppies on those puppies?

110
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,540
As I've stated before on numerous occasions,

111
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,560
the only sea creature I would even consider being eaten by

112
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,790
is the Kraken,

113
00:05:40,790 --> 00:05:42,780
because the last words I would hear are:

114
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,420
"Release the Kraken."

115
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,850
That never gets old.

116
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,160
"Release the Kraken!"

117
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,930
Oh, chills.

118
00:05:50,870 --> 00:05:53,540
Besides, I'm having dinner with Amy.

119
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:56,270
Oh, okay. I'll just go home and be alone.

120
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:57,370
W-Which is cool.

121
00:05:57,370 --> 00:06:00,520
I eat alone, I sleep alone, I cry alone, so...

122
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,750
Cool.

123
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:06,010
Darn.

124
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:08,690
If you weren't busy, I'd ask you to join us.

125
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:12,420
Really? I can come? Thanks!

126
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:14,690
Sheldon, are you sure you want to be bringing Raj

127
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:15,910
on your date night with Amy?

128
00:06:15,910 --> 00:06:17,710
Oh, absolutely.

129
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:22,250
I have a contractual obligation to provide Amy with conversation

130
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:24,160
and casual physical contact,

131
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,890
but nowhere is it specified

132
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:29,040
that I can't outsource that to an Indian.

133
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:35,230
Howie?

134
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:37,090
Howie?

135
00:06:37,090 --> 00:06:40,190
Hey, there's my beautiful bride!

136
00:06:40,190 --> 00:06:41,160
Can you see me?

137
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:43,660
I can. How are you?

138
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,050
I'm amazing.

139
00:06:45,050 --> 00:06:47,450
I mean, this is even better than I dreamed.

140
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:52,180
I look out the window, and... it's all so unbelievable.

141
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:53,550
Good for you.

142
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:56,970
I just had a seemingly endless dinner with your mom.

143
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:01,200
Oh, yeah? That's nice.

144
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:03,910
It was. Until I found out you never told her

145
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:05,400
we're not gonna live with her.

146
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:08,240
Let's talk about that for a minute.

147
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:12,730
Hey, look, this pen is floating.

148
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,360
How crazy is that?

149
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:21,670
You said you told her, but you never did!

150
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:24,990
Okay, okay, I know you're upset, but...

151
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,610
let me share something I've learned since I got here.

152
00:07:30,270 --> 00:07:33,850
You realize how small your problems are

153
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:37,040
when you're looking down on them from space.

154
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,190
Now, come on, that's got to make you feel better.

155
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,360
How clear is the image of me on that screen?

156
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,890
Pretty clear.

157
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,460
Do I look like I feel better?

158
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:51,080
I mean, it's not, like, HD quality.

159
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,540
Listen, mister, you're gonna talk to your mother

160
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,780
and you're gonna fix this, or that thing I said

161
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:58,860
I was gonna do to you the minute you got home,

162
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:01,000
you can do to yourself.

163
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,680
Like he's been doing since he got here.

164
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:15,470
Sheldon, this place is so romantic.

165
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:17,090
Oh, I'm glad you like it.

166
00:08:17,090 --> 00:08:18,480
Raj picked it out.

167
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:22,520
Well, when you see him, tell him I say thank you.

168
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,240
Tell him yourself.

169
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:27,750
Over here!

170
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:32,110
I don't understand. What's he doing here?

171
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,220
I invited him.

172
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:35,440
On our date?

173
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,220
Sheldon, that's not okay.

174
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,780
Yes, it is.

175
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:41,920
There's a loophole in the Relationship Agreement.

176
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:43,690
You found a loophole?

177
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:49,330
Sorry I started without you. I'm a little nervous.

178
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:51,730
It's been a long time since I've been on a date.

179
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,940
I can't believe I bleached my mustache for this.

180
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,180
You should go to my girl.

181
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:59,640
She'll knock out those sideburns for free.

182
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,720
You know, Amy, I don't even think

183
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,990
you and I have had a real conversation.

184
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:13,320
Let's use tonight to get to know each other a little better.

185
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:15,170
You start.

186
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:20,170
Go home.

187
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:21,980
I don't understand.

188
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:23,220
Sheldon, how could you do this?

189
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,980
It's our second anniversary.

190
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,900
It's your anniversary?!

191
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,830
Oh, my God, I had no idea.

192
00:09:29,830 --> 00:09:32,480
Amy, please, let me make this right.

193
00:09:32,490 --> 00:09:33,100
Thank you.

194
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:34,430
My pleasure. Waiter?

195
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,260
A bottle of champagne and three glasses.

196
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:41,130
Oh, boy, isn't this romantic?

197
00:09:41,590 --> 00:09:43,790
Oh, I hope that's a rhetorical question,

198
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,960
because I have no clue.

199
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:50,270
This is great. What's the occasion?

200
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:51,520
No occasion.

201
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,790
You know, things have been a little weird between us,

202
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:56,530
so I wanted to throw together a fun night just for you.

203
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:58,620
- That is so sweet. - I got all your favorites.

204
00:09:58,620 --> 00:09:59,720
Beer, wings, sliders.

205
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:01,350
We can watch the football game.

206
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,270
I even painted my stomach.

207
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:08,010
"Go sports"?

208
00:10:08,010 --> 00:10:09,440
in case you were in the mood for baseball,

209
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:11,120
I didn't want to look ridiculous.

210
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,160
This is awesome. I love it!

211
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:15,200
Good, I'm glad.

212
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,480
Gosh, I worked my ass off today.

213
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,080
This is exactly what I needed.

214
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,630
Great. Just relax and enjoy.

215
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:20,970
Tonight is all about you.

216
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:22,600
Ah, thank you!

217
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:29,110
So, where exactly are we in this relationship?

218
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,540
Oh, come on!

219
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:33,220
I just told you I had a hard day.

220
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:34,970
You're right, I'm sorry. Let's watch the game.

221
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:36,320
Great.

222
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:42,490
I just know the longer we wait to talk about it, the weirder it gets.

223
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:46,200
Sweetie, can I just be the girl tonight?

224
00:10:46,930 --> 00:10:48,300
Absolutely. You're the girl, I'm the guy.

225
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,820
Now, you watch your football game

226
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:52,810
- while I make you a little plate here. - Thank you!

227
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,070
Oh, I'll get it.

228
00:10:57,070 --> 00:10:58,310
Go sports!

229
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:03,290
Hello-lo-lo.

230
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:05,000
What are you doing here?

231
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,270
I thought you were out th Sheldon and Amy.

232
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,920
I was, but it's their anniversary

233
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,190
and I didn't want to be a third wheel,

234
00:11:09,190 --> 00:11:10,500
so I figured I'd come over here

235
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:12,540
and hang out with you and Penny on your date.

236
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,400
Well, it's not really a great time.

237
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,330
Penny and I have some things we need to talk about.

238
00:11:17,330 --> 00:11:19,210
No, we don't! Come on in!

239
00:11:19,910 --> 00:11:21,300
Sweet!

240
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,550
I can't believe I shaved my stomach for this.

241
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,610
Hey, Froot Loops.

242
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:38,220
You got a phone call.

243
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:39,700
Who is it?

244
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,400
A woman who says she's your mother

245
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,820
but sounds like your father.

246
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,600
Hey, Ma.

247
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,670
You know, we could see each other

248
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:53,600
if you turn on the computer.

249
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,930
I'm not going near that fakakta thing.

250
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:58,470
I'll catch a computer virus!

251
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:02,950
You can't catch a computer virus.

252
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:07,800
Oh, so now you're an astronaut and a doctor?

253
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:11,090
What do you want, Ma?

254
00:12:11,090 --> 00:12:14,900
Your wife says you have something important to tell me.

255
00:12:15,690 --> 00:12:18,740
Okay, here it is.

256
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:23,200
Bernadette and I are starting a life together and...

257
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:26,150
Oh, God! You are gonna leave me!

258
00:12:26,170 --> 00:12:27,330
Ma...

259
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,670
It's okay.

260
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:31,140
Your father left me, you left me--

261
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:34,700
I guess I'm just the kind of person people like to leave.

262
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:39,120
It's not... definite.

263
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,300
I'll talk to Bernadette.

264
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,470
Don't bother.

265
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,750
I'll just go sit in a hole in the ground

266
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,930
so I'm no trouble when I die.

267
00:12:48,430 --> 00:12:50,150
Stop it, Ma.

268
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:53,900
I'm sure I can get Bernie to come around.

269
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,050
I knew it!

270
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:57,310
I knew she was behind this!

271
00:12:57,310 --> 00:12:59,840
You listen to me, if you want to be a man,

272
00:12:59,850 --> 00:13:02,730
you can't let a woman tell you what to do!

273
00:13:04,310 --> 00:13:05,850
Okay, okay.

274
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:10,290
I can't believe these people won the Cold War.

275
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:15,680
Now, can we please change the subject?

276
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:16,680
Fine.

277
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,690
Explain why you've been gone so long

278
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:20,770
and I haven't gotten a single letter.

279
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:23,020
Not even a lousy postcard!

280
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:31,870
You know, I'm growing to like American football.

281
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:33,880
Yeah, it's fun, isn't it?

282
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,890
Well...it's not the balls-to-the-wall action of badminton or cricket,

283
00:13:36,890 --> 00:13:37,500
but hey...

284
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,210
what is?

285
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:43,850
All right, who's ready for another beer?

286
00:13:43,850 --> 00:13:45,420
- I'm good.  - No, thank you.

287
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,970
Girls.

288
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:50,570
I am having the nicest time.

289
00:13:50,570 --> 00:13:52,700
You guys are like family to me.

290
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:53,920
You know that, right?

291
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:55,510
That's great. Get out.

292
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,440
What? Why?

293
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,690
Penny and I have some issues we need to talk about.

294
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:02,920
Pish on your issues!

295
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:05,850
You guys are fine.

296
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,920
Yes, you hit some bumps along the way.

297
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,180
I mean, Penny,

298
00:14:09,190 --> 00:14:12,120
you've always known how this man has felt about you,

299
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,650
but you made him grovel for affection.

300
00:14:14,650 --> 00:14:15,780
Okay, hold on...

301
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:16,990
Now, don't blame yourself.

302
00:14:16,990 --> 00:14:19,290
He was a groveler from way back.

303
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:24,690
But the point is, the two of you got past it.

304
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:26,490
And, Leonard, you go and propose

305
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:28,680
to this poor girl in the middle of sex?

306
00:14:28,690 --> 00:14:30,320
That was some weak tea, dude.

307
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,430
Some people might say it was romantic.

308
00:14:34,430 --> 00:14:35,930
Yeah, no.

309
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:40,320
But yet, here you two are, still together.

310
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:43,500
And that's even after you and I had our crazy naked night.

311
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,750
Okay... That's enough.

312
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:46,290
I'm just saying

313
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:48,020
that after everything you've been through,

314
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:50,150
you get to look into each other's eyes

315
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:52,820
and say "I love you."

316
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:54,850
And that's beautiful.

317
00:14:57,670 --> 00:15:00,900
Actually, to this day, she's never really said it.

318
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:04,370
Oh, Penny! That's ridiculous!

319
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,370
You know you love him!

320
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:07,920
You look him in the eyes and you say it.

321
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,920
- Raj...  - Oh, come on,

322
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,000
you know you want to say it. Say it.

323
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:13,190
Say you love him.

324
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,040
Say it!

325
00:15:22,310 --> 00:15:24,360
I really thought she would say it.

326
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:36,450
Have I ever told you you're like a sexy praying mantis?

327
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:40,570
Every time you drink alcohol.

328
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,650
You know what's wonderful about the praying mantis?

329
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:47,350
They devour their mate.

330
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:49,150
Your point being?

331
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:58,750
Dessert is served.

332
00:15:59,590 --> 00:16:02,300
I just had cobbler.

333
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:04,800
You know what?

334
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,590
I'm done with this.

335
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:09,550
W-Where are you going?

336
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:11,150
I'm leaving.

337
00:16:11,150 --> 00:16:12,740
You can't leave.

338
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,180
I need you.

339
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:18,220
You do?

340
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,940
Yes.

341
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:22,180
You're my ride.

342
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:26,890
Sheldon, you either say something meaningful

343
00:16:26,890 --> 00:16:30,420
and from the heart, or you and I are done.

344
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,490
All right.

345
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:37,470
Please.

346
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:42,930
Amy...

347
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:45,440
when I look in your eyes

348
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,650
and you're looking back in mine,

349
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:51,540
everything feels not quite normal,

350
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:54,070
because I feel

351
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:57,940
stronger and weaker at the same time.

352
00:16:57,940 --> 00:17:03,850
I feel excited and, at the same time, terrified.

353
00:17:03,850 --> 00:17:06,190
The truth is,

354
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:09,130
I don't know what I feel, except...

355
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:13,300
I know what kind of man I want to be.

356
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:16,650
Sheldon...

357
00:17:16,650 --> 00:17:18,490
that was beautiful.

358
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:19,650
I should hope so.

359
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,050
That's from the first Spider-Man movie.

360
00:17:26,790 --> 00:17:29,650
I'll take it.

361
00:17:30,470 --> 00:17:31,890
Good.

362
00:17:31,890 --> 00:17:34,270
Now, I assume we're splitting the check?

363
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:39,570
Hey, Stuart.

364
00:17:39,570 --> 00:17:42,720
Oh, hey. I was actually just about to close up.

365
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,050
Oh, I'm sorry. I'll leave.

366
00:17:44,050 --> 00:17:46,010
No, no. It's okay. Hang out.

367
00:17:46,010 --> 00:17:46,720
You sure?

368
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:49,200
Yeah, you're my first customer today.

369
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,350
All right. Great.

370
00:17:51,350 --> 00:17:52,770
I'm, uh, having a nightcap.

371
00:17:52,770 --> 00:17:54,280
You want to join me?

372
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,450
What are you drinking?

373
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:58,450
Coffee liqueur in a Chewbacca mug.

374
00:17:58,450 --> 00:18:01,320
I call it a sad-tini.

375
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:03,900
Perfect for the night I'm having. Thank you.

376
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:07,150
Hmm. Nice not to drink alone.

377
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,820
Amen to that.

378
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:10,500
Sometimes I pour

379
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:13,340
a little chardonnay into my dog's water bowl.

380
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:15,520
You're kidding.

381
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:18,600
She's kind of a mean drunk, but what are you gonna do?

382
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:19,890
Cheers.

383
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,350
Cheers.

384
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:23,120
- A little music? - Sure.

385
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:29,380
Bossa nova.

386
00:18:29,390 --> 00:18:32,970
You listen to that with your hips as well as your ears.

387
00:18:32,970 --> 00:18:34,380
Mmm.

388
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,990
Something about...

389
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:42,420
Latin music just makes me feel like

390
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:45,500
I'm on a white sand beach in Rio.

391
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,380
Yeah.

392
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:52,470
The sun, the waves, the beautiful bodies,

393
00:18:52,470 --> 00:18:56,120
tanned and glistening with sweat.

394
00:19:11,270 --> 00:19:12,970
- I should go. - Yeah.

395
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:16,120
Uh, thank you for the drink.

396
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:18,620
No problem.

397
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:21,460
- Hey, Stuart. - Yeah?

398
00:19:21,470 --> 00:19:24,690
Do you want to... hang out tomorrow night,

399
00:19:24,690 --> 00:19:27,350
maybe grab a bite to eat or catch a late movie?

400
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:31,180
Yeah, I-I'd like to, but I'm a little tight on funds.

401
00:19:31,190 --> 00:19:32,700
No problem. My treat.

402
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:34,290
I'll swing by after work.

403
00:19:34,290 --> 00:19:35,580
Okay.

404
00:19:35,590 --> 00:19:37,220
Okay.

405
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:43,930
I could do worse.

406
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:50,950
Aw, that's such good news, Howie.

407
00:19:50,950 --> 00:19:52,130
Thank you for telling her.

408
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:55,260
Hey, I'm a grown man; I'm gonna live with my wife.

409
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:59,980
My mother's just gonna have to learn to make do on her own.

410
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:01,770
Was she upset?

411
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:05,140
Who can tell? She yells everything.

412
00:20:06,690 --> 00:20:08,960
She might have been upset.

413
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,590
She might have been hungry.

414
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:14,040
Thanks for fixing it.

415
00:20:14,050 --> 00:20:15,230
I love you.

416
00:20:15,230 --> 00:20:16,600
I love you, too.

417
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,810
Sweet dreams. I'll talk to you tomorrow?

418
00:20:18,810 --> 00:20:21,690
Good night, Rocket Man.

419
00:20:21,690 --> 00:20:24,360
To infinity and beyond, baby.

420
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,360
Loops.

421
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:30,870
You realize you just lied your ass off

422
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,980
to your wife and your mother.

423
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,340
I know.

424
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:36,690
What are you gonna do when you get back to Earth?

425
00:20:36,690 --> 00:20:38,670
Oh, I'm never going back.

